### Manual requests for the ComputeSeparation Aspire harness.
### The fake platform sends the platform requests: it assigns the pod on the WorkerProxy, assigns the placeholder Host
### to the app, and links the worker to the Host.
### Its /simulate routes are harness-only; the WorkerProxy and Host routes they call are the real contracts.
###
### Run AppHost with the `project-placeholder-manual` launch profile (F5, or the command below). It pins the ports used
### here and turns off automatic assign and link so you can send each step yourself, in order.
###
###   dotnet run --project tools\ComputeSeparation\AppHost\ComputeSeparation.AppHost.csproj --launch-profile project-placeholder-manual
###
### Opt in to a second distinct proxy/worker on the SAME Host (the default remains one worker):
###   dotnet run --project tools\ComputeSeparation\AppHost\ComputeSeparation.AppHost.csproj --launch-profile project-placeholder-manual -- --ComputeSeparation:EnableSecondWorker=true --ComputeSeparation:SecondWorkerManagementPort=7082
### Only worker1 is auto-linked in profiles with AutoLink=true. Worker2 always waits for the manual steps below.
### For concurrent harness sessions, override all pinned profile/dashboard ports or use --no-launch-profile with
### ComputeSeparation:AutoLink=false and dynamically allocated endpoints; copy Host/FakePlatform URLs from Aspire.

@platform = http://localhost:7060
@host = http://127.0.0.1:7071
@workerProxy = http://localhost:7081
@secondWorkerProxy = http://localhost:7082
@firstWorker = first
@secondWorker = second

### Expected flow, in order.

### 1. The platform assigns the pod on the WorkerProxy. Expect 201, or 204 if repeated.
### 503 WorkerNotReady means the sample worker has not connected yet; retry.
# @name assignFirstWorker
POST {{platform}}/simulate/worker/assign?worker={{firstWorker}}

### Optional: the WorkerProxy pod state is now ReadyForRequest.
GET {{workerProxy}}/admin/worker/state

### 2. The platform assigns the placeholder Host to the app (POST /admin/instance/assign). Expect 202, or 409 if
### repeated. The Host finishes specializing only after step 3 links the worker.
# @name assignHost
POST {{platform}}/simulate/host/assign

### 3. The platform links the worker to the Host. Expect 201, or 200 for a matching retry.
# @name linkFirstWorker
POST {{platform}}/simulate/worker/link?worker={{firstWorker}}

### 4. A client invokes the function through Host -> WorkerProxy -> worker.
# @name invokeBeforeLaterLink
GET {{host}}/api/hello

### Continue only after step 4 returns 200. X-Compute-Worker-Id identifies worker1.
### 5. Assign worker2 independently; retry 503 until its worker connects. Expect 201/204.
# @name assignSecondWorker
POST {{platform}}/simulate/worker/assign?worker={{secondWorker}}

### Optional: inspect the second proxy, not worker1's proxy.
GET {{secondWorkerProxy}}/admin/worker/state

### 6. Link worker2 AFTER worker1 has served the running app. Expect 201, with no ScriptHost restart.
# @name linkSecondWorker
POST {{platform}}/simulate/worker/link?worker={{secondWorker}}

### 7. Repeat the link. Expect 200, same channel; existing workers must not reload their functions.
# @name repeatSecondLink
POST {{platform}}/simulate/worker/link?worker={{secondWorker}}

### 8. Send both requests, and repeat as needed after worker2 finishes function loading.
### Expect 200 and two distinct X-Compute-Worker-Id values (worker2 has the "-2" suffix).
### Host selects ready workers round-robin; the public invocation API does not support targeting a worker.
### FakePlatform logs the selected worker ID for assignments/links; Aspire has separate proxy/worker logs.
# @name invokeAfterLaterLinkA
GET {{host}}/api/hello

###
# @name invokeAfterLaterLinkB
GET {{host}}/api/hello
